   "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/SnowSky1/universal-imagegen-agent/zipball/v0.1.2",
   "body": "## Install v0.1.2\r\n\r\nThis release contains the image-count fix and a follow-up packaging fix that preserves both npm CLI entries. Version 0.1.2 is now published on npm through GitHub Actions trusted publishing, with a signed provenance statement:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nnpm install --global universal-imagegen-agent@0.1.2\r\nimagegen-agent --version\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe npm archive, Python wheel, and source distribution are also attached.\r\n\r\n## Fixed\r\n\r\n- Node.js generate/edit now reject explicit `n=0` instead of silently requesting one image. Omitted counts still default to one; valid counts 1–10 are unchanged.\r\n- Both npm executable paths use the canonical `bin/...` form so current npm does not remove them during publish normalization.\r\n\r\n## Added\r\n\r\n- Shared image-count fixtures for Node.js and Python CLIs.\r\n- A runnable generate → edit local API integration walkthrough, with explicitly labeled fixture images and real-provider instructions.\r\n- A provider-feedback issue form and clearer verification boundaries.\r\n\r\n## Verified\r\n\r\n- 19 Node.js tests and 32 Python tests, plus syntax/lint/format checks.\r\n- Python wheel/sdist build and npm package-content review.\r\n- Local generation/editing integration and zero-count rejection before a provider request.\r\n- The packaged npm artifact installs in a separate directory; both commands return 0.1.2 and the installed CLI rejects `--n 0` with exit code 2.\r\n- Publish dry-run no longer removes the CLI entries.\r\n- The npm registry package was independently installed and verified: both CLI aliases report 0.1.2, zero is rejected, and the packaged local integration example passes.\r\n\r\nLive-model image quality has not been validated for this release. The bundled PNG outputs are integration fixtures.\r\n"
  },
