   "body": "## Install v0.1.1\r\n\r\nThis intermediate release has been superseded by [v0.1.2](https://github.com/SnowSky1/universal-imagegen-agent/releases/tag/v0.1.2), which is available on npm and also fixes npm CLI-entry normalization. The attached 0.1.1 package remains available for reproducibility:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nnpm install --global https://github.com/SnowSky1/universal-imagegen-agent/releases/download/v0.1.1/universal-imagegen-agent-0.1.1.tgz\r\n```\r\n\r\nA Python wheel and source distribution are also attached. The npm package was installed in a separate directory and its CLI returned `imagegen-agent 0.1.1`.\r\n\r\n## Fixed\r\n\r\n- Node.js generate/edit now reject an explicit `n=0` instead of silently requesting one image. Omitted counts still default to one; valid counts 1–10 are unchanged.\r\n- Shared image-count fixtures cover both CLIs, including generate/edit, omitted values, zero, negative values, and the upper limit.\r\n\r\n## Added\r\n\r\n- A runnable local generate → edit API integration example, packaged with npm, with explicit fixture-output labeling.\r\n- Real-provider walkthrough, verification boundaries, and a provider-feedback issue form.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- Node.js syntax checks and 19 tests passed locally.\r\n- Python lint/format checks and 32 tests passed locally.\r\n- The local integration example passed; Python wheel/sdist and npm package contents were checked.\r\n\r\nLive-provider image quality was not exercised in this release verification.\r\n"
  },
