   "body": "## Universal ImageGen Agent v0.1.0\n\nFirst public release of the Codex-derived image generation workflow for general-purpose AI agents.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Reuse the Codex imagegen prompt engineering, use-case taxonomy, edit invariants, and prompt library in any shell-capable agent.\n- Install a zero-Python Node.js CLI through npm or pnpm.\n- Install the bundled `universal-imagegen` agent skill with one command.\n- Generate, edit, and batch images through configurable OpenAI-compatible Images APIs.\n- Connect compatible Qwen-Image deployments through a gateway or provider adapter.\n- Keep the Python CLI and library for Python-native integrations.\n\n### Install\n\n```bash\nnpm install --global universal-imagegen-agent\n# or\npnpm add --global universal-imagegen-agent\n```\n\nInstall the accompanying agent skill:\n\n```bash\nimagegen-agent install-skill\n```\n\nRun without a global install:\n\n```bash\nnpx universal-imagegen-agent --version\npnpm dlx universal-imagegen-agent --version\n```\n\n### Links\n\n- npm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/universal-imagegen-agent\n- Repository: https://github.com/SnowSky1/universal-imagegen-agent"
